{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And the mountains were covered.</b> Therefore 'all flesh expired' — for they found no place to flee and died." "<b>Fifteen cubits above did the waters prevail, etc.</b> This verse teaches us, by force of plain reasoning, that the ark was submerged in the water only six cubits. How so? From where do we know that fifteen cubits above the waters prevailed? Rather, when you count the seventy-two days there are from the 17th of Marcheshvan, on which the ark came to rest, until the 1st of Tevet, on which the mountaintops appeared — in them the ark was that much submerged in the water. You will understand to where the waters had reached, for it is an easy thing to recognize in wood that has sat in water many days even after it has dried. And one may say that they saw and recognized that it had been submerged in the water only six cubits, which it had lost during those seventy-two days, and they reckoned that the decrease comes to one cubit per twelve days. And according to this calculation they went back and counted the one hundred and eighty days there are from the 28th of Sivan, on which the rains ceased and the waters began to decrease, until the 1st of Tevet, on which the mountaintops appeared, and found in them fifteen parts of twelve days per part. And the two extra days need not be scrutinized, for the shortfall in their reckoning comes to only a sixth of a part. And since they saw from the submersion of the ark that the decrease comes to one cubit per twelve days, they understood that fifteen cubits above did the waters prevail, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:24.760080532Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}